{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 42,
  "title": "Size and shape",
  "description": "Say how big something is and what shape it is.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Size and shape are the first things you say about an object, and they are ordinary adjectives and nouns.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El tamaño, el peso and el largo are masculine. La medida and la altura are feminine. El largo means the length of a thing, and la altura means how tall it is. La medida is also what you do when you measure something.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el tamaño",
            "en": "the size"
          },
          {
            "es": "la altura",
            "en": "the height"
          },
          {
            "es": "el peso",
            "en": "the weight"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The adjectives",
        "body": "Largo, corto, ancho, estrecho, redondo and cuadrado all describe a shape or a size, and they go straight after the noun: una mesa redonda, un artículo estrecho. Es and está both work: la mesa es redonda means the table is round, and la mesa está sucia means the table is dirty.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "una mesa redonda",
            "en": "a round table"
          },
          {
            "es": "un callejón estrecho",
            "en": "a narrow street"
          },
          {
            "es": "el cuadrado es grande",
            "en": "the square is big"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
